cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its measurements, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Agentic Trader: an advisory US-equity research agent that grades its own calls"
authors:
  - family-names: Shoham
    given-names: Omer
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/omershoham/claude-trader"
abstract: >-
  An advisory-only US stock research system. A quant screen on point-in-time SEC
  fundamentals and a survivorship-aware universe narrows ~1,500 stocks to a shortlist,
  a local LLM classifies news into a fixed catalyst vector, and an LLM researches the
  finalists. Every recommendation is graded forward, net of costs, against the
  equal-weight universe and a screen-only control; backtests report a Deflated Sharpe
  ratio against every configuration tried. It never places trades.
keywords:
  - quantitative finance
  - point-in-time data
  - backtesting
  - large language models
  - equity research
  - SEC EDGAR
